sequenceDiagram
  participant Q as cx.notifications
  participant C as Consumer
  participant RQ as cx.notifications.retry (TTL 5 s)
  participant DLQ as cx.notifications.dlq
  Q->>C: deliver event E (attempt 1)
  C->>C: process fails (retryable)
  C->>RQ: publish copy, header x-attempt=1, wait for confirm
  C->>Q: basicAck original (only after confirm)
  Note over RQ: message sits for TTL, then dead-letters to default exchange with key cx.notifications
  RQ->>Q: expired message re-enters queue
  Q->>C: deliver E (attempt 2)
  C->>C: fails again ... until attempt 5
  C->>C: markDead(E) persisted in notif_processed_event
  C->>DLQ: basicReject(requeue=false) routes via cx.events.dlx
  Note over DLQ: Operator inspects, fixes cause, re-drives. Consumers stay idempotent on eventId.
